## Loot (`LOOT`, `assign_loot`, `roll_loot`)
- Tiers follow WoW item quality: Poor, Common, Uncommon, Rare, Epic.
- `assign_loot()` runs once in `main()`. It stores each monster's Uncommon gear in `ASSIGNED_LOOT`.
- `roll_loot()` runs after a normal win. Roll = d100 + (monster AC - 8). Under 31 drops nothing. Poor and Common drop a generated weapon. Uncommon drops the assigned gear. A Rare or Epic roll on a normal monster drops Uncommon gear instead.
- A boss kill rolls one more d100: 1-70 nothing, 71-90 a Rare named weapon, 91-100 an Epic named weapon. The weapon goes in the bag.
- min_roll / gold value: Poor 31/8, Common 61/25, Uncommon 81/60, Rare 94/150, Epic 100/400.
- Option 5 bag lists `[Weapon]` / `[Armor]` / `[Junk]` and can equip weapon or armor slots.

## Shop
- Menu option 6. Options 1-4 stay as they are.
- Potion cost is `25 + (level - 1) * 15`, restores 10 HP, drunk immediately.
- Each visit rolls two shop offers: Uncommon (60%) / Rare (30%) / Epic (10%), each a weapon or armor. Buy prices 150 / 350 / 900. No Poor or Common in the shop.
- Option 4 sells one bag item. Sell values: Poor 8, Common 25, Uncommon 60, Rare 150, Epic 400. Option 5 leaves.

## Fight actions
- If the hero has a `wins` key: prompt `1) Attack  2) Flee`. Flee rolls d20 vs `10 + (ac - 8) // 2`. Fail takes armored damage. Checker heroes without `wins` auto-attack (one d20 / one d10).

## Save file (`saves/checkpoint.txt`)
- One `key=value` per line.
- `name` and `weapon` are strings. `bag` is a string joined with `|`. Everything else is an int.
- `load_checkpoint` returns only the keys in the file. After Continue, `fill_hero` fills weapon, attack bonus, bag, wins, level, and max HP when an old save is missing them.

## Menu
1 Fight, 2 View hero, 3 Save, 4 Quit, 5 View loot bag, 6 Visit the shop, 7 Rest, 8 Read battle log, 9 Load a hero.

The menu prints three labels across, with four spaces between columns. Reading order is left to right.

Continue with no `saves/checkpoint.txt` starts a new hero. A damaged checkpoint (ValueError on load) also starts a new hero. Option 9 treats a damaged hero file the same way and keeps the current hero. Option 5 lists the bag. A number equips that item when it is a weapon, and the old weapon goes back into the bag. 0 leaves the bag. Option 7 Rest heals 10 HP, and HP never goes above max HP. Option 8 prints `saves/battle_log.txt`. A fight prints one random room line before the taunt. Every fight then writes `saves/checkpoint.txt`. There is no y/n save question. Option 3 also writes `saves/<hero>.txt` (spaces removed from the name) and records that file in `saves/heroes.txt`. Option 9 loads one of those hero files.

A hit in the battle log reads `Name was hit by the Monster for N damage.` If that hit drops HP to 0 or below, the next log line is `Name collapsed and woke up back at camp.` HP is set back to max HP before the auto-save.
